arning  income as a property manager the annells  recently had to make the difficult  decision to ask relatives for help it's  embarrassing i don't like it  oh my goodness and claudia fears the  rest of the country has already moved on  it's just a long time  and people are tired and i don't think  people or the government or anybody  is really all that worried about  how people are getting by anymore  you rack your brain for an explanation  for why two years in you're at a  financial low point what do you come up  with  definitely no assistance  for a time when this country definitely  needs help more than 72 million  americans say they are struggling to pay  their expenses a number that's actually  grown by about 2 million people a month  since last august  and it's not hard to understand why with  inflation at a fresh 40-year high  the average american family is paying an  extra 250 dollars every month just to  live like they used to  pretty much everything's going up but  not our  not our pay  so you know it's it's it's very  difficult to not be mad the family had  been getting by thanks to the government  stimulus checks and extended  unemployment benefits and when we spoke  to them a year into the pandemic claudia  in particular felt seen and supported i  don't feel as  skeptical as i did last year because  last year i just really felt like wow  we're just going to be in an island you  know  but this year i feel like okay  i think the government is hearing us and  trying  to get somewhere but now those benefits  are gone and like so many other middle  class families the anells have had to  cut back don't go out anymore  drive as the least amount as possible  because gas prices are insane  oil prices for the house not doubled but  pretty close wow so you know now we're  very very very frugal  what about food  like we told our son no more snacks  and all of the essentials now you know  odd jobs like seasonal delivery driver  and garage attendant have helped but  only some  17 15 hour full-time job is not going to  pay any bills it's not going to pay  anything you know it's only going to  help if you have another job on top of  that and even with occasional freelance  audio work that pays much much better  the family is falling behind definitely  all credit card payments are not  happening credit card payments are just  not happening they're just not going to  happen right now not even the minimum no  i can't even make the minimum  because i'm prioritizing for car  payments  mortgage payments oil payments  gasoline to get to these jobs gabe is  still hopeful his old job will bounce  back eventually but until it does the  inels like so many other families are in  a state of economic  and emotional distress  it makes me angry it makes me feel  defeated  and it's hard to watch my husband go  through it because he is a very  very intelligent person he's a very  capable person  he's a hard worker um  and  it's just unfair to have everything just  sort of taken away when we first spoke  to you  you thought maybe this would be over in  three months maybe six nine months with  something that was being floated  did you ever in a million years think  we'd be here two years later  no as a matter of fact we were very  hesitant about doing this because we  were like do people really want to keep  hearing about how terrible everyone's  doing  you know it felt like kicking a horse  while it's down kind of thing  and we decided yeah because it's  important because maybe people don't  realize that it's still happening maybe  people are in their own bubble  and feeling like everything's hunky-dory  now and it's not  so it's it's definitely not as a matter  of statistical fact hunky-dory right now  census numbers were like one in three  families struggling to pay their bills  our poll out this morning says most  americans are concerned about paying  their bills and it's all about where you  started and you're trying to hold on to  where you were so he's saying 1750 is  not paying his bills for someone else  that's good enough right he's sliding  down the economic ladder and he's afraid  and a lot of americans have that fear  right now here's where i was two years  ago and i'm dying to hold on and i feel  myself sliding back it's scary it's  relative to your financial circumstance  but i'm slipping and it feels like i'm  drowning right now in the deep end  exactly and understand their frustration  and pain especially if you hear the  biden administration say things are  better you know that the economy is on  the upswing things are better so i  admire the fact that he said we were  reluctant to do it and then we thought  no we really need to tell people there  are still a lot of people in trouble a  lot and a lot of people still even if  your wages went up if inflation is  higher than your wages you actually got  a pay cut yeah what's his original job  audio he was an audio engineer for big  corporate events and they haven't  bounced back well i will say the company  that he used to work for hired one of  the two workers back so he may get some  good news in the days ahead we'll see  we're hoping yeah or another company or  another company a lot of people can  identify with that family these are  stories that we need to hear yeah
 

